Privacy Policy — SmartZ Clipboard
Last updated: May 7, 2026

The short version
SmartZ Clipboard stores your clipboard history locally on your device only.
We also receive anonymised crash reports and aggregate usage analytics from Microsoft to help us fix bugs and improve the app. You are always in full control of your clipboard data.

1. Who we are
SmartZ Clipboard is a local clipboard manager published on the Microsoft Store and developed as an independent application. For privacy-related enquiries, contact us at chriszigounas2@gmail.com.

Scope of this policy: This policy applies to the SmartZ Clipboard app only. Microsoft's own Privacy Statement governs the Microsoft Store, payment processing, and any data Microsoft collects as an independent data controller when you download or purchase the app. We and Microsoft act as separate, independent data controllers — we are not joint controllers.

2. What clipboard data we access
To provide its core functionality, SmartZ Clipboard monitors and reads the contents of your Windows clipboard each time you copy something. This may include:

Data type	Description
Text	Any text you copy from any application
Images	Screenshots or images copied to the clipboard
File paths	Names and paths of files you copy in Windows Explorer
3. How we process your clipboard data
Clipboard content is processed entirely on your device to:

Save items to a local history so you can retrieve them later
Automatically categorise items — for example, detecting 4–6 digit codes as PINs, recognising URLs, and identifying file types — to make searching and filtering easier
Display thumbnail previews of images
All categorisation logic runs locally using pattern matching. Clipboard content is never transmitted to any server.

4. Where your clipboard data is stored
All clipboard history is stored in a SQLite database file on your local machine:

%APPDATA%\SmartZ Clipboard\clips.db
Copied images are saved as files in the same folder. Your settings (hotkey, theme, startup preference) are stored in settings.json in the same location. Clipboard content never leaves your device.

5. Diagnostic data from Microsoft
When you use SmartZ Clipboard via the Microsoft Store, Microsoft may provide us with the following aggregated, platform-level data through our Partner Center dashboard:

Data type	Purpose
Error Reporting Data	Anonymised crash logs and error diagnostics collected by Windows, used to identify and fix bugs
App Analytics	Aggregate, non-personal usage statistics such as daily active users, acquisition counts, and ratings, used to understand how the app is used and to guide improvements
This data is provided by Microsoft in aggregated or anonymised form. We do not receive your name, Microsoft account details, or any clipboard content through these reports. Microsoft governs the collection of this data under their own privacy statement.

6. What we do NOT do
We do not transmit your clipboard content to any server
We do not build individual user profiles or track you personally
We do not create user accounts or require sign-in
We do not sell data to third parties
We do not access the clipboard of other users or other applications
7. Your rights and controls
Action	How
Delete individual clips	Hover a clip and click ×, or right-click → Delete
Clear all history	Use the "Clear" button in the toolbar
Full removal	Uninstall the app — this removes all local data
8. Legal basis for processing
We process your clipboard data on the basis of legitimate interest — specifically to provide the clipboard management service you have explicitly installed and chosen to run. The monitoring only occurs while the application is running and can be stopped at any time by closing or uninstalling it.

9. Children's privacy
SmartZ Clipboard does not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13. The app processes only locally-generated clipboard content and does not involve user accounts or online services directed at children.

10. Changes to this policy
If we make material changes to this policy, we will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page and may notify you via a banner inside the app.

11. Contact
Email: chriszigounas2@gmail.com

We aim to respond within 5 business days.

